# Requiem for an &quot;Independent Remedy&quot;: The Civil Rights Acts of 1866 and 1971 as Remedies for Employment Discrimination

**Authors:** Reiss, Michael

## Abstract
The availability and usefulness of the Civil Rights Acts of 1866 and 1971 in the employment discrimination context are analyzed by examining their scope and coverage, the nature of the remedies they afford, and their procedural requirements in comparison with each other and with Title VII. (LBH)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ178036

